theorem.content:
\label{yu-theorem-9-01-1}
    Let $\kappa\in\mathbb{R}\setminus\{0\}$ and $\tau>0$. Suppose that Assumptions $(A_1)$-$(A_3)$ hold. Then the following statements are equivalent:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item[$(i)$] The pair $[A,B]$ is rapidly stabilizable.
  \item [$(ii)$] The pair $[A,B]_{\kappa,\tau}$ is rapidly stabilizable.
  \item [$(iii)$] The pair $[A,B]_{\kappa,\tau}$ is  rapidly stabilizable with  instantaneous-valued feedback.
\end{enumerate}

