\label{thm:main-intro}
	Let $\mathbf{V}$ be a pseudovariety of semigroups.
	The following are equivalent.
	\begin{bracketenumerate}
		\item The pseudovariety $\mathbf{V}$ affords efficient compression.
		\item The pseudovariety $\mathbf{V}$ contains neither $\mathbf{LRB}$, $\mathbf{RRB}$, nor $\mathbf{T}$.
		\item The pseudovariety $\mathbf{V}$ admits straight-line programs of length $\mathcal{O}(\smash{\log}^2 N)$.
	\end{bracketenumerate}
  Furthermore, if all groups in $\mathbf{V}$ are solvable, then the above are equivalent to $\mathbf{V}$ admitting straight-line programs of length $\mathcal{O}(\log N)$ as well as of width $\mathcal{O}(1)$ and length $\mathcal{O}(\polylog N)$.

