\label{thm:0}
Let $\mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{D}$ be tensor categories, and let subcategories $\mathcal{A} \subset \mathcal{C}$ and $\mathcal{B} \subset \mathcal{D}$ be abelian categories with finitely many isomorphism classes of simple objects. Assume further that $\mathbf{D}^b(\mathcal{A})$ and $\mathbf{D}^b(\mathcal{B})$ are left triangulated tensor ideals of $\mathbf{D}^b(\mathcal{C})$ and $\mathbf{D}^b(\mathcal{D})$, respectively.
